IMPORT `ei2-work-sharing-and-courses`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), ss 27 and 28: disqualification in general, and how long it lasts and
-- when it is served. Piece ei2. Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current
-- to 2026-09-30. Seat: the claimant.
--
-- Relations (Hohfeld), stated once. A disqualification is the Act's removal of the claimant's claim to benefits for
-- the weeks it covers: the Commission has a privilege not to pay (and a power to determine how many weeks, within
-- the Act's limits, s 28(1)); the claimant has no claim to benefits for those weeks and is liable to the Commission's
-- determination of their number.
--
-- What the Act leaves to the Commission or to a judgment is an input, never worked out here: whether the claimant had
-- "good cause"; whether an employment is "suitable" (the criteria are for regulations: s 54(k.1), reg 9.002, piece er1);
-- whether a direction was "reasonable"; and the number of weeks the Commission determines under s 28(1).
--
-- Sections 27(2) and (3) are repealed ([Repealed, 2016, c. 12, s. 102] and [Repealed, 2012, c. 19, s. 605], src:724-725):
-- there is nothing to encode.

§ `Section 27(1) - disqualification in general`

-- (a): "has not applied for a suitable employment that is vacant after becoming aware that it is vacant or becoming
-- vacant, or has failed to accept the employment after it has been offered to the claimant".
-- src:711 | (a) has not applied for a suitable employment that is vacant after becoming aware that it is vacant or becoming vacant, or has failed to accept the employment after it has been offered to the claimant;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 27(1)(a) (src:711)
GIVEN `the claimant has not applied for a suitable employment that is vacant, after becoming aware that it is vacant or becoming vacant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has failed to accept a suitable employment after it has been offered to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 27(1)(a) not applying for or accepting a suitable employment` IF
       `the claimant has not applied for a suitable employment that is vacant, after becoming aware that it is vacant or becoming vacant`
    OR `the claimant has failed to accept a suitable employment after it has been offered to the claimant`

-- src:712 | (b) has not taken advantage of an opportunity for suitable employment;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 27(1)(b) (src:712)
GIVEN `the claimant has not taken advantage of an opportunity for suitable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 27(1)(b) not taking advantage of an opportunity for suitable employment` IF
    `the claimant has not taken advantage of an opportunity for suitable employment`

-- (c): the direction must be one "given to the claimant by the Commission with a view to assisting the claimant to find
-- suitable employment, if the direction was reasonable having regard both to the claimant's circumstances and to the
-- usual means of obtaining that employment". Reasonableness is a judgment: a BOOLEAN input.
-- src:713 | (c) has not carried out a written direction given to the claimant by the Commission with a view to assisting the claimant to find suitable employment, if the direction was reasonable having regard both to the claimant’s circumstances and to the usual means of obtaining that employment; or
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 27(1)(c) (src:713)
GIVEN `the Commission has given the claimant a written direction with a view to assisting the claimant to find suitable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has not carried out the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction was reasonable having regard both to the claimant's circumstances and to the usual means of obtaining that employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 27(1)(c) not carrying out a written direction of the Commission` IF
        `the Commission has given the claimant a written direction with a view to assisting the claimant to find suitable employment`
    AND `the claimant has not carried out the direction`
    AND `the direction was reasonable having regard both to the claimant's circumstances and to the usual means of obtaining that employment`

-- (d): the interview is one the Commission directed "to enable the Commission or another appropriate agency (i) to
-- provide information and instruction to help the claimant find employment, or (ii) to identify whether the claimant
-- might be assisted by job training or other employment assistance".
-- src:714 | (d) has not attended an interview that the Commission has directed the claimant to attend to enable the Commission or another appropriate agency
-- src:715 | (i) to provide information and instruction to help the claimant find employment, or
-- src:716 | (ii) to identify whether the claimant might be assisted by job training or other employment assistance.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 27(1)(d) (src:714-716)
GIVEN `the Commission has directed the claimant to attend an interview` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interview is to enable the Commission or another appropriate agency to provide information and instruction to help the claimant find employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interview is to enable the Commission or another appropriate agency to identify whether the claimant might be assisted by job training or other employment assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has not attended the interview` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 27(1)(d) not attending an interview directed by the Commission` IF
        `the Commission has directed the claimant to attend an interview`
    AND (   `the interview is to enable the Commission or another appropriate agency to provide information and instruction to help the claimant find employment`
         OR `the interview is to enable the Commission or another appropriate agency to identify whether the claimant might be assisted by job training or other employment assistance`)
    AND `the claimant has not attended the interview`

-- The lead-in: "A claimant is disqualified from receiving benefits under this Part if, without good cause since the
-- interruption of earnings giving rise to the claim, the claimant (a) ... (b) ... (c) ... or (d) ...". "Good cause" is
-- not defined in the Act: the gate is a judgment input, "the claimant did so without good cause".
-- src:708 | Disqualification and Disentitlement
-- src:709 | Disqualification — general
-- src:710 | 27 (1) A claimant is disqualified from receiving benefits under this Part if, without good cause since the interruption of earnings giving rise to the claim, the claimant
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 27(1) (src:708-710)
GIVEN `without good cause since the interruption of earnings giving rise to the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not applying for or accepting a suitable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not taking advantage of an opportunity for suitable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not carrying out a written direction of the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not attending an interview directed by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 27(1) the claimant is disqualified from receiving benefits under Part I` IF
        `without good cause since the interruption of earnings giving rise to the claim`
    AND (   `not applying for or accepting a suitable employment`
         OR `not taking advantage of an opportunity for suitable employment`
         OR `not carrying out a written direction of the Commission`
         OR `not attending an interview directed by the Commission`)

§ `Section 27(1.1) - termination of a referral`

-- (a) "the Commission or an authority that the Commission designates has, with the agreement of the claimant, referred
-- the claimant to a course or program of instruction or training or to any other employment activity for which
-- assistance has been provided under an employment support measure other than one referred to in paragraph 59(c)".
-- src:717 | Termination of referral
-- src:718 | (1.1) A claimant is disqualified from receiving benefits under this Part if
-- src:719 | (a) the Commission or an authority that the Commission designates has, with the agreement of the claimant, referred the claimant to a course or program of instruction or training or to any other employment activity for which assistance has been provided under an employment support measure other than one referred to in paragraph 59(c); and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 27(1.1)(a) (src:717-719)
GIVEN `the Commission or an authority that the Commission designates has, with the agreement of the claimant, referred the claimant to a course, program or other employment activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment support measure under which assistance was provided, if any` IS A MAYBE `ei2 Kind of employment support measure`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 27(1.1)(a) a referral with the claimant's agreement to an activity assisted under a measure other than one in paragraph 59(c)` IF
        `the Commission or an authority that the Commission designates has, with the agreement of the claimant, referred the claimant to a course, program or other employment activity`
    AND `ei2 s 59 there is a measure and it is not of the kind` `the employment support measure under which assistance was provided, if any` `ei2 s 59(c) measure providing employment assistance services`

-- (b) "the Commission has terminated the referral because (i) without good cause, the claimant has not attended or
-- participated in the course, program or employment activity and, in the opinion of the Commission, it is unlikely that
-- the claimant will successfully complete it, (ii) without good cause, the claimant has withdrawn from it, or (iii) the
-- organization providing it has expelled the claimant". "In the opinion of the Commission" is the Commission's
-- judgment: a BOOLEAN input.
-- src:720 | (b) the Commission has terminated the referral because
-- src:721 | (i) without good cause, the claimant has not attended or participated in the course, program or employment activity and, in the opinion of the Commission, it is unlikely that the claimant will successfully complete the course, program or employment activity,
-- src:722 | (ii) without good cause, the claimant has withdrawn from the course, program or employment activity, or
-- src:723 | (iii) the organization providing the course, program or employment activity has expelled the claimant.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 27(1.1)(b) (src:720-723)
GIVEN `the Commission has terminated the referral` IS A BOOLEAN
      `without good cause the claimant has not attended or participated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the Commission it is unlikely that the claimant will successfully complete it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `without good cause the claimant has withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the organization providing it has expelled the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 27(1.1)(b) the Commission has terminated the referral for one of the stated reasons` IF
        `the Commission has terminated the referral`
    AND (   (`without good cause the claimant has not attended or participated` AND `in the opinion of the Commission it is unlikely that the claimant will successfully complete it`)
         OR `without good cause the claimant has withdrawn`
         OR `the organization providing it has expelled the claimant`)

-- src:718 | (1.1) A claimant is disqualified from receiving benefits under this Part if
-- src:719 | (a) the Commission or an authority that the Commission designates has, with the agreement of the claimant, referred the claimant to a course or program of instruction or training or to any other employment activity for which assistance has been provided under an employment support measure other than one referred to in paragraph 59(c); and
-- src:720 | (b) the Commission has terminated the referral because
-- src:721 | (i) without good cause, the claimant has not attended or participated in the course, program or employment activity and, in the opinion of the Commission, it is unlikely that the claimant will successfully complete the course, program or employment activity,
-- src:722 | (ii) without good cause, the claimant has withdrawn from the course, program or employment activity, or
-- src:723 | (iii) the organization providing the course, program or employment activity has expelled the claimant.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 27(1.1) (src:718-723)
GIVEN `a referral with the claimant's agreement to an activity assisted under a measure other than one in paragraph 59(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has terminated the referral for one of the stated reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 27(1.1) the claimant is disqualified from receiving benefits under Part I` IF
        `a referral with the claimant's agreement to an activity assisted under a measure other than one in paragraph 59(c)`
    AND `the Commission has terminated the referral for one of the stated reasons`

§ `Section 28(1) - how many weeks`

-- "A disqualification under section 27 is for the number of weeks that the Commission may determine, but (a) the
-- number of weeks of a disqualification arising under paragraph 27(1)(a) or (b) shall be not fewer than 7 or more than
-- 12; and (b) ... under paragraph 27(1)(c) or (d) or subsection 27(1.1) shall be not more than 6." The Commission's
-- determination is an input; the Act's limits are figures.
-- src:726 | Duration of disqualification
-- src:727 | 28 (1) A disqualification under section 27 is for the number of weeks that the Commission may determine, but
-- src:728 | (a) the number of weeks of a disqualification arising under paragraph 27(1)(a) or (b) shall be not fewer than 7 or more than 12; and
-- src:729 | (b) the number of weeks of a disqualification arising under paragraph 27(1)(c) or (d) or subsection 27(1.1) shall be not more than 6.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 28(1) (src:726-729)
GIVEN ground IS A `ei2 Ground of disqualification under section 27`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 28(1) the fewest weeks of disqualification the Act allows` IS
    CONSIDER ground
    WHEN `ei2 s 27(1)(a) not applying for, or not accepting, a suitable employment`        THEN JUST 7
    WHEN `ei2 s 27(1)(b) not taking advantage of an opportunity for suitable employment`   THEN JUST 7
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:726 | Duration of disqualification
-- src:727 | 28 (1) A disqualification under section 27 is for the number of weeks that the Commission may determine, but
-- src:728 | (a) the number of weeks of a disqualification arising under paragraph 27(1)(a) or (b) shall be not fewer than 7 or more than 12; and
-- src:729 | (b) the number of weeks of a disqualification arising under paragraph 27(1)(c) or (d) or subsection 27(1.1) shall be not more than 6.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 28(1) (src:726-729)
GIVEN ground IS A `ei2 Ground of disqualification under section 27`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 28(1) the most weeks of disqualification the Act allows` IS
    CONSIDER ground
    WHEN `ei2 s 27(1)(a) not applying for, or not accepting, a suitable employment`        THEN 12
    WHEN `ei2 s 27(1)(b) not taking advantage of an opportunity for suitable employment`   THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 6

-- src:726 | Duration of disqualification
-- src:727 | 28 (1) A disqualification under section 27 is for the number of weeks that the Commission may determine, but
-- src:728 | (a) the number of weeks of a disqualification arising under paragraph 27(1)(a) or (b) shall be not fewer than 7 or more than 12; and
-- src:729 | (b) the number of weeks of a disqualification arising under paragraph 27(1)(c) or (d) or subsection 27(1.1) shall be not more than 6.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 28(1) (src:726-729)
GIVEN ground IS A `ei2 Ground of disqualification under section 27`
      `the number of weeks that the Commission determines` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 28(1) the number of weeks determined is within the limits of the Act` IS
        `the number of weeks that the Commission determines` AT MOST `s 28(1) the most weeks of disqualification the Act allows` ground
    AND (CONSIDER `s 28(1) the fewest weeks of disqualification the Act allows` ground
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST fewest THEN `the number of weeks that the Commission determines` AT LEAST fewest)

§ `Section 28(2) to (7) - when it is served, carried forward and deferred`

-- (2): "Subject to subsections (3) to (5), the weeks of disqualification are to be served during the weeks following the
-- waiting period for which benefits would otherwise be payable if the disqualification had not been imposed and, for
-- greater certainty, the length of the disqualification is not affected by any subsequent loss of employment by the
-- claimant during the benefit period." The week's place in the run of those weeks is an input (1 for the first);
-- weeks on which serving is deferred under subsection (5) are not counted in that run and are not served (fork ei2-F2
-- in NOTES.md). The subsequent loss of employment is not an input, because the text says it changes nothing.
-- src:730 | When disqualification is to be served
-- src:731 | (2) Subject to subsections (3) to (5), the weeks of disqualification are to be served during the weeks following the waiting period for which benefits would otherwise be payable if the disqualification had not been imposed and, for greater certainty, the length of the disqualification is not affected by any subsequent loss of employment by the claimant during the benefit period.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 28(2) (src:730-731)
GIVEN `the number of weeks of disqualification` IS A NUMBER
      `the place of this week among the weeks following the waiting period for which benefits would otherwise be payable if the disqualification had not been imposed` IS A NUMBER
      `the serving of the disqualification is deferred for this week under subsection 28(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 28(2) the week is served as a week of disqualification` IF
        (NOT `the serving of the disqualification is deferred for this week under subsection 28(5)`)
    AND `the place of this week among the weeks following the waiting period for which benefits would otherwise be payable if the disqualification had not been imposed` AT LEAST 1
    AND `the place of this week among the weeks following the waiting period for which benefits would otherwise be payable if the disqualification had not been imposed` AT MOST `the number of weeks of disqualification`

-- (5): "The Commission shall defer the serving of the disqualification if the claimant is otherwise entitled to special benefits or
-- benefits by virtue of section 25." "Special benefits" are the keel's `s 2(1) special benefits` (benefits for any reason but the
-- regular one), so the caller gives the reason for the benefits the claimant would otherwise get. Benefits "by virtue of
-- section 25" are those of s 25(1) (this piece).
-- src:736 | Deferral
-- src:737 | (5) The Commission shall defer the serving of the disqualification if the claimant is otherwise entitled to special benefits or benefits by virtue of section 25.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 28(5) (src:736-737)
GIVEN `the claimant is otherwise entitled to benefits for the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reason for those benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits`
      `the claimant is otherwise entitled to benefits by virtue of section 25` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 28(5) the serving of the disqualification is deferred` IF
       (`the claimant is otherwise entitled to benefits for the week` AND `s 2(1) special benefits` `the reason for those benefits`)
    OR `the claimant is otherwise entitled to benefits by virtue of section 25`

-- (4): the limit of 700 hours.
-- src:734 | Limitation
-- src:735 | (4) No weeks of disqualification shall be carried forward against a claimant who has had 700 or more hours of insurable employment since the event giving rise to the disqualification.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 28(4) (src:734-735)
GIVEN `the hours of insurable employment the claimant has had since the event giving rise to the disqualification` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 28(4) no weeks of disqualification are carried forward` IF
    `the hours of insurable employment the claimant has had since the event giving rise to the disqualification` AT LEAST 700

-- (3): "Any portion of the disqualification that has not been served when the claimant's benefit period ends shall,
-- subject to subsections (4) and (5), be served in any benefit period subsequently established within two years after
-- the event giving rise to the disqualification." The benefit period is taken to be established on its first day
-- (fork ei2-F3 in NOTES.md); "within two years after" ends on the second anniversary of the event, which counts (the keel's
-- fork F4). The new benefit period is assumed to be a subsequent one: the caller supplies only its first day.
-- src:732 | Disqualification to be carried forward
-- src:733 | (3) Any portion of the disqualification that has not been served when the claimant’s benefit period ends shall, subject to subsections (4) and (5), be served in any benefit period subsequently established within two years after the event giving rise to the disqualification.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 28(3) (src:732-733)
GIVEN `the day of the event giving rise to the disqualification` IS A DATE
      `the first day of a benefit period subsequently established` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 28(3) a benefit period is established within two years after the event` IF
        `the first day of a benefit period subsequently established` AT LEAST `the day of the event giving rise to the disqualification`
    AND `the first day of a benefit period subsequently established` AT MOST (`add years` `the day of the event giving rise to the disqualification` 2)

-- src:732 | Disqualification to be carried forward
-- src:733 | (3) Any portion of the disqualification that has not been served when the claimant’s benefit period ends shall, subject to subsections (4) and (5), be served in any benefit period subsequently established within two years after the event giving rise to the disqualification.
-- src:734 | Limitation
-- src:735 | (4) No weeks of disqualification shall be carried forward against a claimant who has had 700 or more hours of insurable employment since the event giving rise to the disqualification.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 28(3), s 28(4) (src:732-735)
GIVEN `the number of weeks of the disqualification not served when the benefit period ends` IS A NUMBER
      `the day of the event giving rise to the disqualification` IS A DATE
      `the first day of a benefit period subsequently established` IS A DATE
      `the hours of insurable employment the claimant has had since the event giving rise to the disqualification` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 28(3) the weeks of disqualification carried forward into the later benefit period` IS
    IF     `s 28(3) a benefit period is established within two years after the event` `the day of the event giving rise to the disqualification` `the first day of a benefit period subsequently established`
       AND (NOT (`s 28(4) no weeks of disqualification are carried forward` `the hours of insurable employment the claimant has had since the event giving rise to the disqualification`))
    THEN `the number of weeks of the disqualification not served when the benefit period ends`
    ELSE 0

-- (6): "For the purposes of this Part, benefits are deemed to be paid for the weeks of disqualification."
-- src:738 | Presumption
-- src:739 | (6) For the purposes of this Part, benefits are deemed to be paid for the weeks of disqualification.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 28(6) (src:738-739)
GIVEN `the week is a week of disqualification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 28(6) benefits are deemed to be paid for the week` IS
    IF `the week is a week of disqualification`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (7): "Subsection (6) does not apply to prevent a claimant from requesting that a benefit period established for the
-- claimant as a minor attachment claimant be cancelled under subsection 10(6) and that a benefit period be established
-- for the claimant as a major attachment claimant to enable the claimant to receive special benefits." The request is
-- s 10(6)'s (out of range: section 10(6), piece ei1); here only that s 28(6) is no bar to it.
-- src:740 | Exception
-- src:741 | (7) Subsection (6) does not apply to prevent a claimant from requesting that a benefit period established for the claimant as a minor attachment claimant be cancelled under subsection 10(6) and that a benefit period be established for the claimant as a major attachment claimant to enable the claimant to receive special benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 28(7) (src:740-741)
GIVEN `a benefit period was established for the claimant as a minor attachment claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is that it be cancelled under subsection 10(6) and that a benefit period be established as a major attachment claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is to enable the claimant to receive special benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 28(7) the deeming of benefits as paid is no bar to the request` IS
    IF     `a benefit period was established for the claimant as a minor attachment claimant`
       AND `the request is that it be cancelled under subsection 10(6) and that a benefit period be established as a major attachment claimant`
       AND `the purpose is to enable the claimant to receive special benefits`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
